      <p>
        Short-stay rentals in India get checked by local authorities, sometimes on short notice.
        That check needs a guest's ID on file. Before the website, that meant collecting IDs
        manually into a WhatsApp group — reliable most of the time, harder to search fast during a
        busy period. Now ID capture happens as part of booking itself, attached permanently to that
        guest's record instead of a message thread. That reliability is also why the underlying
        data gets backed up as JSON — peace of mind, built in.
